    "updated_at": "2023-08-02T12:45:40Z",
    "body": "> I'm doing some research how the spec changed over years, but I can't find snapshots earlier than 2015.\r\n\r\nYes, we did not build any snapshots earlier than then. Sorry!\r\n\r\n> Also IMHO the FAQ could use a link to the snapshots instead of just referring to them:\r\n\r\nThe FAQ is not specific to the HTML Standard, so instead it tells you how to find them on any WHATWG standard.\r\n\r\n> And wouldn't it be useful when yearly reports (snapshot end of year) are made publicly available preferable with diffs, so you can easily link to the yearly changes in the spec (as a simple stakeholder accountability).\r\n\r\nNo, we do not have any special status for any given commit. Each commit is as transient as any other. If you would like to prefer certain ones for your personal use (e.g. weekly, yearly, every SHA that starts with \"f\"), you can, but no such schedule is endorsed by the WHATWG.",
