    "updated_at": "2023-08-02T13:08:34Z",
    "body": "> The FAQ is not specific to the HTML Standard, so instead it tells you how to find them on any WHATWG standard.\r\n\r\nNot really easy to find IMHO,  an example link like there is for translating would be helpful.  \r\nhttps://whatwg.org/faq#translating\r\n\r\n> Yes, we did not build any snapshots earlier than then. Sorry!\r\n\r\nBut can't it still be done? Isn't that what a version control system is all about?\r\n\r\nI know there is no special status for commits, but still there is a spec end of every year. \r\n\r\nSee it this way, nearly every organizations provide accountability for stakeholders about their yearly operations: **what have we achieved this year**? \r\n\r\nIMHO it would be valuable if WHATWG does that too, (it's just some plain scripting I guess). (But maybe it's a Github feature somewhere I don't know about.)",
