    "updated_at": "2023-08-02T13:12:58Z",
    "body": "> But can't it still be done?\r\n\r\nI'm not sure! You can certainly read the source (that's what the version control system is about), but as for whether the old spec will build... well, please give it a try and report back, if you'd like!\r\n\r\n> See it this way, nearly every organizations provide accountability for stakeholders about their yearly operations: **what have we achieved this year**?\r\n\r\nYou can use GitHub to see all commits or merged pull requests in a given time period if you'd like to see what we've accomplished. We don't feel a need to show it proactively.",
